## Don't Do (Yet)
- Payment integration (Paystack) - post-MVP
- SMS authentication - post-MVP
- Email notifications - post-MVP
- Automated reminders - post-MVP
- Chat/messaging between clients and pros - post-MVP

## Key Design Principles
- **Mobile-first**: Most users in Namibia will be on mobile
- **Fast loading**: Keep bundle size small, optimize images
- **Simple UX**: Don't overthink - make it obvious how to use
- **Trust signals**: Show ratings, verification badges prominently
- **Clear CTAs**: "Book Now" buttons should be unmissable

## Common Patterns

### Fetching Data:
```javascript
// Use Supabase client for all database operations
const { data, error } = await supabase
  .from('professionals')
  .select('*, services(*)')
  .eq('verification_status', 'approved')
```

### Image Upload:
```javascript
// Upload to Supabase Storage
const { data, error } = await supabase.storage
  .from('portfolio-images')
  .upload(`${userId}/${fileName}`, file)
```

### Protected Routes:
```javascript
// Check auth status in middleware or component
const { data: { user } } = await supabase.auth.getUser()
if (!user) redirect('/login')
```

## Notes for Claude Code
- Start with the easy foundational stuff first
- Build the booking engine structure but don't get stuck on complex availability calculations - we'll refine that algorithm together
- Focus on getting basic CRUD operations working before optimizing
- Use shadcn/ui components if helpful for UI (buttons, forms, dialogs)
- When in doubt, keep it simple - MVP means minimum viable
- Always enable RLS policies when creating tables
- Test with seed data as you build
